## Why This Is Asked
This tests designing a scalable CAPA program for multi-tenant real-time pipelines with cross-region controls and regulatory considerations, not just a checklist.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence lineage and PII flags
- Region- and tenant-aware state machine
- Minimal REST API for evidence-linked CAPAs
- Per-tenant metrics and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback for CDC changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model (Typescript)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  schemaVersion: string;
  eventId?: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  traces: string[];
  timestamp: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'contained'|'mitigated'|'verified'|'closed';
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement data lineage capture across CDC and streaming layers?
- What rollback safety checks would you add to the canary plan?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests translating CAPA into actionable steps for a concrete, repeatable risk. It targets beginner CAPA skills without vague theory.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model design
- Lifecycle/state machine
- Evidence capture and traceability
- Lightweight REST API for CAPAs
- Canary-based remediation and region-aware metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let cas = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const cap = {...req.body, id: Date.now().toString(), status: 'detected'};
  cas.push(cap);
  res.status(201).json(cap);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the CAPA workflow end-to-end?
- How would you enforce secret masking in build logs across agents?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for a hardware-leaning, safety-critical system with OTA risk, cross-region data, and telemetry traces. Emphasizes traceability, regionalization, and safe validation.

## Key Concepts
- Immutable evidence ledger (incidentId, firmwareVersion, OTA bundle, sensor flags, region, vehicle_type)
- Region-aware CAPA lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API to link CAPAs with logs/traces
- Region- and vehicle-type metrics: recurrence rate, MTTR, false-positive rate
- RCA template and canary rollout with rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express route to create a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks } = req.body;
  // Persist CAPA object with linked evidence in DB (pseudo)
  const capaId = generateId();
  saveCapa({ capaId, incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks, status: 'DETECTED' });
  res.status(201).json({ id: capaId });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model cross-region deduplication of CAPAs when two regions report the same incident?
- What metrics and experiments would verify the efficacy of the canary rollout before global deployment?

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates practical CAPA thinking for data quality issues in streaming workloads, focusing on deduplication, regional containment, and fail-safes.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model
- Lifecycle state machine
- Evidence linkage
- Canary-based remediation
- Region-based metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Express API to create CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let capas = [];

app.post('/capas', (req, res) => {
  const capa = { id: capas.length + 1, ...req.body, status: 'Observed' };
  capas.push(capa);
  res.status(201).json(capa);
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the candidate's ability to define a data-driven CAPA program for supply-chain vulnerabilities in multi-region systems, balancing traceability, regional scoping, and automated rollout.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data modeling with SBOM, CVEs, tenants, regions
- Region-aware lifecycle state machines
- Minimal REST API for CAPA creation/update with logs/traces
- Metrics for containment, recurrence, MTTR
- RCA templates and canary rollout controls

